      "summaries": {
        "en": "AGENTS.md is an open specification that provides a standardized way to guide AI coding assistants through complex development tasks. It works by defining clear, structured instructions in markdown format that help agents understand context, break down problems, and maintain consistency across sessions. Developers can use it to create reusable agent templates for common workflows like API integration or refactoring, making AI-assisted coding more predictable and collaborative. Try implementing it in your TypeScript projects to see how structured prompts improve agent performance.",
        "zh": "AGENTS.md 是一个开源规范，为AI编程助手提供标准化指导格式，解决复杂开发任务中指令不一致的问题。它通过Markdown结构化定义任务上下文、步骤和约束，让AI代理能更好地理解意图、分解问题并保持会话连续性。其核心在于将模糊需求转化为可执行的指导框架，开发者可创建可复用的模板来处理API集成或代码重构等常见场景。尝试在TypeScript项目中应用此格式，你会发现结构化提示能显著提升AI协作的可靠性和效率。",
        "es": "AGENTS.md is an open specification that provides a standardized way to guide AI coding assistants through complex development tasks. It works by defining clear, structured instructions in markdown format that help agents understand context, break down problems, and maintain consistency across sessions. Developers can use it to create reusable agent templates for common workflows like API integration or refactoring, making AI-assisted coding more predictable and collaborative. Try implementing it in your TypeScript projects to see how structured prompts improve agent performance.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "agents.md gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "AGENTS.md is an open specification that provides a standardized way to guide AI coding assistants through complex development tasks. It works by defining clear, structured instructions in markdown format that help agents understand context, break down problems, and maintain consistency across sessions. Developers can use it to create reusable agent templates for common workflows like API integration or refactoring, making AI-assisted coding more predictable and collaborative. Try implementing it in your TypeScript projects to see how structured prompts improve agent performance.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/agentsmd/agents.md for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
