      "summaries": {
        "en": "AionUi is a free, local, open-source interface that simplifies working with multiple AI coding assistants like Gemini CLI, Claude Code, and Codex. It provides a unified environment where developers can seamlessly switch between different AI tools without managing separate setups. You can install it locally to experiment with various coding assistants, compare their outputs, and integrate them into your development workflow for tasks like code generation, debugging, or learning new programming concepts.",
        "zh": "AionUi是一款免费、本地化、开源的界面工具，旨在整合多种AI编程助手（如Gemini CLI、Claude Code、Codex等），解决开发者需频繁切换不同工具的繁琐问题。它通过统一的操作环境，让用户能在一个平台内调用多个AI模型，无需单独配置每个服务。技术上，该项目基于TypeScript开发，注重模块化设计，便于扩展新的AI工具集成。开发者可将其部署在本地环境中，用于代码生成、调试辅助或学习编程，通过对比不同AI的输出结果来优化工作流程，适合探索AI编程助手实际应用的实验场景。",
        "es": "AionUi is a free, local, open-source interface that simplifies working with multiple AI coding assistants like Gemini CLI, Claude Code, and Codex. It provides a unified environment where developers can seamlessly switch between different AI tools without managing separate setups. You can install it locally to experiment with various coding assistants, compare their outputs, and integrate them into your development workflow for tasks like code generation, debugging, or learning new programming concepts.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "AionUi stands out for acp, ai, and ai-agent in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "AionUi is a free, local, open-source interface that simplifies working with multiple AI coding assistants like Gemini CLI, Claude Code, and Codex. It provides a unified environment where developers can seamlessly switch between different AI tools without managing separate setups. You can install it locally to experiment with various coding assistants, compare their outputs, and integrate them into your development workflow for tasks like code generation, debugging, or learning new programming concepts.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/iOfficeAI/AionUi for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
